WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:08.050
One of the things that is so
amazing about this show

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.093
is how formidable the actors are.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:12.346
And one of the true
highlights of the season

00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:13.972
is the scene
where you have

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:15.349
Reese and Marcia Gay Harden.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.643
You're the truth teller.
Was that true?

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:20.145
Being in any scene with
Marcia Gay Harden

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:23.106
you have to stay on
your toes, because she will

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:26.652
pivot and turn on you and
you better be prepared! 

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.446
It's so fun to have
her as a scene partner.

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:31.657
I think that people change.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:33.867
I think people grow.

00:00:34.785 --> 00:00:38.205
I know I'm evolving,
I wonder if you are.

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:40.749
I love that Bradley gets to say

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:42.542
that I think we have
to make room for

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.835
people to change and grow.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.296
Watching these two titans

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:48.090
face off and have
this conversation.

00:00:48.215 --> 00:00:49.800
Do you have to cancel Alex?

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.426
Is that what we're here to do?

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.553
Or is there an opportunity
for forgiveness?

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.265
It's at the root of what a lot
of people are thinking right now, 

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:57.724
but not very many
people are saying.

00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:00.644
You're not going to Mitch
Kessler's memorial are you?

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:02.562
I am.

00:01:02.646 --> 00:01:03.355
With Yanko

00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:05.399
I had to come up with
sort of a backstory as to

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:07.776
why does he feel the need
to go to the service

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:08.944
knowing what this man has done?

00:01:09.403 --> 00:01:11.697
I think he's probably there for
Mitch's kids to say, 

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.156
I knew your dad a long time

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:15.367
and I think on a moral level he
needs to do that for himself.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.536
My youngest asked me

00:01:17.995 --> 00:01:19.454
if all of dad's friends
would be there?

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:23.000
I think these characters
have a choice to make - 

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.377
really asking themselves
when our heroes

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:26.670
end up being more villainous.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.755
Then we thought, well how am I
gonna respond to this?

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.132
And I think true to life

00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:32.718
some people decide
that I'm going to

00:01:32.718 --> 00:01:36.179
respond to the man that I know
the man that was in front of me.

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:42.019
I wasn't gonna come but I
just kept feeling that I had to

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:47.274
and to say a few words about
Mitch and what he meant to me.

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:51.153
For Alex, she sacrifices
her legacy in a way

00:01:51.153 --> 00:01:54.531
by going to the funeral
and speaking the truth.

00:01:54.656 --> 00:01:57.909
I think it's the beginning
of a big shift for her.

00:01:58.452 --> 00:01:59.494
I'm gonna be cancelled, 

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:01.872
Cory, for things that I did.

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:04.791
Alex I think feels
pretty much at the bottom

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.126
of the barrel as a human being.

00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:08.920
The loss of her only friend,

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.297
soulmate on the planet.

00:02:10.464 --> 00:02:12.299
Her hypocrisy within herself, 

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:15.594
what she asked him to do --
the guilt of that.

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:17.638
It's like that thread
in a sweater

00:02:17.638 --> 00:02:19.765
that's just getting
pulled and it's just gonna

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:21.725
unravel and unravel and unravel

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:23.143
until she finally
just kind of...

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:25.062
You'll see.

